Article 2 (Requirements for Application)
(1) An application for registration under these Rules shall satisfy all of the following requirements:
1. All existing land registers shall have been closed and new land registers prepared for newly developed land on the basis of cadastral confirmation surveys following completion of a land development project;
2. The registered owners of the former parcels of land shall all be the same person;
3. The registration records of the former land shall contain no registration of rights other than ownership.
(2) Notwithstanding paragraph (1) 3, an application for registration under these Rules may be filed in any of the following cases:
1. Where all registration records of the former land contain trust registrations with identical registered particulars under the subparagraphs of Article 81 (1) of the Registration of Real Estate Act;
2. Where all registration records of the former land contain supplementary registrations of prohibitions under Article 61 (3) of the Housing Act;
3. Where registration records of the former land contain registrations of superficies, rights to lease on a deposit basis, leasehold rights, or easements over servient land (land providing the benefit);
4. Where all registration records of the former land contain registrations of mortgages or maximum-amount mortgages with identical causes and dates of registration and identical receipt numbers.
